TYPES.md §3.7, §8.2, §11.5: a case of a local variant used as a type (`Shape.circle`) names the local variant, and a dependent map's value type is exposed like any field type: E2111 at each; the dependent map's domain is an expression, not exposed.
-- a/a.canon --
package a

local variant Shape {
  circle { r: Int }
  square
}

local record Stone {
  n: Int
}

/// An item.
record Item {
  /// Its count.
  n: Int = 1
}

/// The items.
let items: table Item = {
  one {}
}

/// A holder.
record Holder {
  /// Its circle.
  s: Shape.circle
  /// A stone per item.
  byItem: {i in items: Stone} = {}
}
-- findings.txt --
error[E2111]  a/a.canon:26:6
  Holder is public but exposes the local type Shape: make Shape public or Holder local

error[E2111]  a/a.canon:28:24
  Holder is public but exposes the local type Stone: make Stone public or Holder local

2 errors, 0 warnings in 1 package (…)
